{title: 307 - I Am Coming to the Cross}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Gospel}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Am]I am coming to the [C7/Bb]cross; I am [Dm/A]poor [F]and weak and [Am]blind;
[Am]I am counting all [C]but [Am]dross; I shall full salvation [C7/Bb]find.
[Dm/A]I am trusting, Lord, in [F]Thee. O thou Lamb of Calvary;
[F/A]Humbly at Thy cross I [C7/Bb]bow. Save me, [F]Jesus, save me [Am]now.

Refrain:
[Am]I am trusting, Lord, in [C]Thee.
[Am]O thou Lamb of Calvary;
[Dm/A]Humbly at Thy cross I [F]bow.
[F]Save me, Jesus, save me now.

Verse 2:
[Am]Long my heart [C7/Bb]has sighed [F]for Thee;
[Am]Long has evil reigned within;
[Dm/A]Jesus sweetly [F]speaks to me:
[F/A]'I will cleanse [C7/Bb]you from [F]all sin.'

Verse 3:
[Am]Here I give [C7/Bb]my all [F]to Thee:
[Am]Friends and time and earthly [C7/Bb]store;
[Dm/A]Soul and body [F]Thine to be,
[F/A]Wholly Thine [C7/Bb]forevermore.

Verse 4:
[Am]Jesus comes! [C7/Bb]He [Dm/A]fills [F]my soul!
[Am]Perfected in Him I [C7/Bb]am;
[Dm/A]I am every [F]whit made whole:
[F/A]Glory, glory [C7/Bb]to [F]the Lamb!
